sections:

#### prop_section ####
kind: proposition
----
statement: If an [even] number neither is one of those which is continually doubled from a dyad, nor has its half odd, then it is both even-times even and even-times odd.
----
proof:

Let the [even] number {A} neither be one of those doubled from a dyad, nor have its half odd.

I say that {A} is both even-times-even and even-times-odd.

